@startuml
!include ./nora-medlink-style.puml
title Figure 3.8 — Nora MedLink Sequence Diagram: Medicine Reminder

actor Patient
participant "Next.js Reminder View" as Frontend
participant "FastAPI Reminder API" as API
participant "Auth Dependency" as Auth
database "PostgreSQL Database" as DB
participant "Notification Record" as Notification
participant "Notification Channel" as Channel

Patient -> Frontend : Enter reminder title and due time
opt Browser push token available
  Frontend -> API : POST /reminders/fcm-token
  API -> Auth : get_current_user(token)
  Auth --> API : Authenticated user
  API -> DB : Upsert NotificationToken
  DB --> API : Token saved
end
Frontend -> API : POST /reminders
API -> Auth : get_current_user(token)
Auth --> API : Authenticated user
API -> DB : Insert Reminder(status=UPCOMING)
DB --> API : Reminder id
API -> Notification : Build scheduled notification
Notification -> DB : Insert Notification(status=SCHEDULED)
DB --> API : Reminder and notification saved
API --> Frontend : Created reminder
Frontend --> Patient : Display scheduled reminder
... At scheduled due time ...
Channel -> DB : Read due scheduled notification
Channel --> Patient : Deliver reminder notification
@enduml
